[{:db/id "q-18266/selection/4d7eed95e6988f947f34d5f5baa83ed5399cb85091423a6533c322015c294b3e" :answer/id #uuid "71fd57f9-e530-5a97-b60c-4a731a184abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3,k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" :answer/id #uuid "63239bfa-abc2-5456-b72c-36c1ad52197d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266/selection/2164ccfa5a79bc4208d739a14881266daa9d1222c58e48f26c06f3970f7744c7" :answer/id #uuid "bc06fc4f-c7fc-5893-b461-e459ca368289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2,k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" :answer/id #uuid "3615ddb6-e41f-5ac3-a45a-3ea8d821b22b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266/selection/c2a2884376d46933ed7222b177d528dafd7a9a5c5b4f7eeed501a1f1d7d4bd83" :answer/id #uuid "f3182a92-607d-5d08-b485-57ccb8fa8949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1,k=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "675d7932-f3f5-5edb-9e6d-615469e579ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18266/selection/4d7eed95e6988f947f34d5f5baa83ed5399cb85091423a6533c322015c294b3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-18266/selection/4d7eed95e6988f947f34d5f5baa83ed5399cb85091423a6533c322015c294b3e" "q-18266/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" "q-18266/selection/2164ccfa5a79bc4208d739a14881266daa9d1222c58e48f26c06f3970f7744c7" "q-18266/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" "q-18266/selection/c2a2884376d46933ed7222b177d528dafd7a9a5c5b4f7eeed501a1f1d7d4bd83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18266" :question/id #uuid "ed79892d-8665-5eea-9da5-c71f18c14bb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-18266" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors  $p=⟨0,-1,-{k}^{2}⟩,q=⟨2,4,8⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,-1,5⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -{k}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|+(-{k}^{2})\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(2\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 8)-{k}^{2}(2\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =18-2{k}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 18-2{k}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =9 \\\\ k & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-3$ or $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18266/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18266"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "a967dc66-0118-5493-ba6b-ed185a2f39b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" :answer/id #uuid "cfb08fc4-d8a3-54d5-bb54-a1c75677494d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "a1619f76-7ca5-5fae-9492-f532ebca3b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3527c645-e657-5c5b-91b7-8aafa5c18edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "0536971c-3be2-5c83-b4a3-d789cd629211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "945d7554-314d-5b49-9757-96fb4bb8caea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73748/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-73748/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-73748/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" "q-73748/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-73748/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-73748/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73748" :question/id #uuid "17da1f0b-bc64-50f2-8f48-1593c355e2c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73748" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,-1,0)$, $B(-1,2,-1)$, $C(1,1,2)$, and $D(3,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j-k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =i+k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-6+9+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|\\,5\\,|=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection/1966de14618afd727582fd6ed7d1c111fb3a97358a016aa542834244a408f710" :answer/id #uuid "3e512bb4-19d4-522b-8254-4942d85e8651" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection/866a26b3e05a58aca03b0e904241688a206b2eeec34614e8be5c7f771e3e5674" :answer/id #uuid "d94a2ea2-d392-5bf1-a66f-2b3aecf615e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=-\\sqrt{3}$ or $k=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection/6d82331f17b5280bae525c2735599f9ecfeefb274a531eaeae6cd740795c8f53" :answer/id #uuid "ca7aaac4-d229-56ac-a8d4-e35d627bd041" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection/1135fb152e7631ab3c3ef072d203a35e9c3d6310cf8411b587c3b3bfe12ce729" :answer/id #uuid "ae00f325-17b1-5d6c-b134-dce9c59fe394" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=\\sqrt{6}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection/1326ea674ebbbff71f75c0260f971d47974e4e45de90cee281a867641745beaa" :answer/id #uuid "66469620-af9b-594f-99b4-376af1e1a470" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=-6$ or $k=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92b7663e-dfcb-5f8f-b6fb-5573fce1a4ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128461/selection/6d82331f17b5280bae525c2735599f9ecfeefb274a531eaeae6cd740795c8f53" :answer-field/choices ["q-128461/selection/1966de14618afd727582fd6ed7d1c111fb3a97358a016aa542834244a408f710" "q-128461/selection/866a26b3e05a58aca03b0e904241688a206b2eeec34614e8be5c7f771e3e5674" "q-128461/selection/6d82331f17b5280bae525c2735599f9ecfeefb274a531eaeae6cd740795c8f53" "q-128461/selection/1135fb152e7631ab3c3ef072d203a35e9c3d6310cf8411b587c3b3bfe12ce729" "q-128461/selection/1326ea674ebbbff71f75c0260f971d47974e4e45de90cee281a867641745beaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128461" :question/id #uuid "41e53fe4-b06e-5150-a976-5badf29f5d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128461" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨{k}^{2},7,4⟩,$ $b=⟨6,7,4⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,0,2⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(7\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)-7(6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4)+4(6\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 7) \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}+0-84 \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}-84 \\\\  & =14({k}^{2}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 14({k}^{2}-6) & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =6 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128461/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128461"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280314/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "b8f92c8b-a6ca-5197-8ba2-88d0ec9022bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280314/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "da4b8e6a-7733-570c-8e3a-1ee5268d7268" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280314/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-280314/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280314" :question/id #uuid "66da7212-a246-5e38-9a80-39fb6123472c" :question/math-academy-id "q-280314" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(3,-2,1),$ $C(-1,4,-1),$ and $D(2,1,0).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+4j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(8-1)+2(-4-1)+3(-2-4) \\\\  & =14-10-18 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-14|=14.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-280314/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
